# DPDP Local Agent — network configuration (Phase 3B skeleton).
# Copy to agent/.env and adjust. All values are OPTIONAL; the secure defaults are
# loopback-only with an empty origin allowlist. Nothing here is a secret in 3B.

# 1) Where the agent LISTENS (bind address). Secure default: 127.0.0.1.
#    Never auto-defaults to 0.0.0.0. Set a LAN/enterprise address explicitly only
#    when you understand the exposure (see README — non-loopback mode).
# GATEWAY_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# GATEWAY_BIND_PORT=7071

# LAN testing example (Agent on another machine, reachable from a laptop's browser):
# GATEWAY_BIND_HOST=192.168.1.50
# GATEWAY_BIND_PORT=7071

# 2) Which web ORIGINS may call the agent. EXACT origins, comma-separated. No '*'.
#    Default is empty (no browser origin allowed until configured).
# GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://app.your-dpdp-host.example

# 3) Where the agent reaches the DPDP CONTROL PLANE (Azure). Not used in Phase 3B.
# GATEWAY_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://control.your-dpdp-host.example
